    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "50cd6805-d326-3f1a-9a25-b899db2a751d",
                "word": "echolocation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d31bd647-3cee-42ab-bd6d-74591bb2f37f",
                        "entry_id": "50cd6805-d326-3f1a-9a25-b899db2a751d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "echolocations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "885a70b9-e2d7-369c-bded-9717d8cfe562",
                        "entry_id": "50cd6805-d326-3f1a-9a25-b899db2a751d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The use of echoes to detect objects as observed in bats and other natural creatures."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75f84ae1-e1f4-4181-af93-c6ea358ddf03",
                                "sense_id": "885a70b9-e2d7-369c-bded-9717d8cfe562",
                                "text": "Since there is no convenient term available to describe this process of locating obstacles by means of echoes, I suggest the word echolocation[…]. The meaning of this word, and a corresponding verb to echolocate, are likely to be clear when first heard or read, since they are formed simply by joining echo and locate. It seems best to accent the first syllable in order to make clear that the word echo is employed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "415c1ba9-c485-4189-b0b1-43aae7987d24",
                                "sense_id": "885a70b9-e2d7-369c-bded-9717d8cfe562",
                                "text": "Now similarly with the aquatic mammals, we know that they can make sounds. We are beginning to get information—although no curves yet—on their sensitivity of hearing. These need to be followed up and we should look for this process of echo-ranging or echolocation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "589497c7-cc85-4263-99eb-4b28d0f80ec2",
                                "sense_id": "885a70b9-e2d7-369c-bded-9717d8cfe562",
                                "text": "Earless ghost swift moths become “invisible” to echolocating bats by forming mating clusters close (less than half a meter) above vegetation and effectively blending into the clutter of echoes that the bat receives from the leaves and stems around them."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f2939876-bf44-4fde-9f81-baae954e8625",
                        "source_entry_id": "50cd6805-d326-3f1a-9a25-b899db2a751d",
                        "source_sense_id": "885a70b9-e2d7-369c-bded-9717d8cfe562",
                        "source_sense_description": "use of echos to detect objects",
                        "target_lang_word": "echolokace",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "echolokace",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ff529ad-1b15-3a16-acb1-906d147474f3",
                                        "entry_id": "4d005327-e8b3-3f19-b81a-9e57578fc836",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "orientace v prostoru pomocí vysílání a přijímání odražených ultrazvuků"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cd8e948-2a30-4217-a20f-521d0eb0eaf6",
                                                "sense_id": "9ff529ad-1b15-3a16-acb1-906d147474f3",
                                                "text": "Patnáctá konference o netopýrech se zabývá nejnovějšími informacemi o evoluci těchto zvířat, echolokaci netopýrů nebo například způsobu jejich ochrany a soužití netopýra s člověkem."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "217785df-e78b-4b9c-b822-eef5de1ac9ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "50cd6805-d326-3f1a-9a25-b899db2a751d",
                        "source_sense_id": "885a70b9-e2d7-369c-bded-9717d8cfe562",
                        "source_sense_description": "use of echos to detect objects",
                        "target_lang_word": "écholocation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "écholocation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "448ab982-30a4-3549-a61e-c50ffd7cc327",
                                        "entry_id": "29a7da9d-3d05-300d-83e9-3009f9187809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Méthode par laquelle certains animaux peuvent visualiser leur environnement en émettant des ondes sonores et en analysant leurs échos."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "908a6dd6-68c3-4310-ae50-94312d2de109",
                                                "sense_id": "448ab982-30a4-3549-a61e-c50ffd7cc327",
                                                "text": "Les êtres vivants qui utilisent l’écholocation (comme les chauves-souris, les baleines et les marsouins) obtiennent des informations sur la taille, la localisation et le mouvement des objets en émettant […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efd252d2-1405-4096-b7a1-63e39fd244be",
                                                "sense_id": "448ab982-30a4-3549-a61e-c50ffd7cc327",
                                                "text": "Cet animal s'oriente dans l’espace par écholocation : il émet des sons de très haute fréquence et utilise l’écho renvoyé par les obstacles ou les proies pour les localiser."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a80aa21-3bf9-363d-b0ab-d5a5bad07c82",
                                        "entry_id": "29a7da9d-3d05-300d-83e9-3009f9187809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Collecte d’informations sur un environnement en analysant l’écho que les obstacles renvoient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f88a26cd-81a0-484b-b201-285b9c7e7205",
                                                "sense_id": "3a80aa21-3bf9-363d-b0ab-d5a5bad07c82",
                                                "text": "Les quatre premiers chapitres sont consacrés, […], aux différents types d'instruments utilisés […], en particulier à la localisation des engins par rapport au fond par écholocation ou par d'autres techniques, faisant essentiellement appel à l'expérience acquise par les auteurs au cours de leurs recherches."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
